      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In APA 7th edition, you use \"et al.\" in all citations for sources with two or fewer authors, but for three or more authors, you cite only the first author followed by \"et al.\" regardless of the total number. Chicago style, however, varies based on your specific note system; for the notes-bibliography method, you always list all co-authors in full the first time and use only the first author thereafter, while the author-date system mimics APA by using \"et al.\" for three or more authors. Simply put, if you are writing in APA, stop listing names after three authors, but if using Chicago's notes system, keep listing them until the second citation appears.",
